1
00:00:22,240 --> 00:00:24,880
The ultimate hunk

2
00:00:27,020 --> 00:00:30,960
Leaping lightly over this hectic era

3
00:00:32,900 --> 00:00:37,440
Diving into the city,
playing at being a hero

4
00:00:37,440 --> 00:00:39,580
I wanna spend time with you for a night

5
00:00:39,580 --> 00:00:45,100
As you keep wearing
nothing but trendy things,

6
00:00:45,100 --> 00:00:49,220
because your bare face looks twice as good

7
00:00:49,740 --> 00:00:50,980
Let it rain

8
00:00:51,760 --> 00:00:58,240
Everybody can do it.
The dreams we set off chasing never stop

9
00:00:58,240 --> 00:01:03,240
Let's head into tomorrow too, new world

10
00:01:04,080 --> 00:01:10,800
Everybody can do it. Even if you stick out a little,
it doesn't hurt

11
00:01:10,800 --> 00:01:18,000
Holding onto restless curiosity,
we're getting stronger and higher

12
00:01:21,680 --> 00:01:22,660
Ahhhhhh

13
00:01:28,850 --> 00:01:31,220
Super rich, lovely

14
00:01:31,220 --> 00:01:31,780
Mm

15
00:01:35,320 --> 00:01:35,940
Mm

16
00:01:35,940 --> 00:01:36,960
Mm

17
00:01:36,960 --> 00:01:37,540
Mm

18
00:01:38,540 --> 00:01:39,160
Mm

19
00:01:39,160 --> 00:01:40,340
Mm

20
00:01:40,340 --> 00:01:41,460
Mm

21
00:01:41,460 --> 00:01:41,940
Mm

22
00:01:52,080 --> 00:01:53,840
What's wrong, little girl?

23
00:01:53,840 --> 00:01:55,460
I'm hungry.

24
00:01:56,160 --> 00:01:58,160
You haven't eaten lunch yet?

25
00:01:58,820 --> 00:01:59,260
Yeah.

26
00:01:59,260 --> 00:02:00,280
Mommy's...

27
00:02:29,980 --> 00:02:31,280
Mind your own business.

28
00:02:31,280 --> 00:02:34,080
What right do you have to interfere?

29
00:02:34,620 --> 00:02:36,940
It's none of your concern, is it?

30
00:02:41,640 --> 00:02:42,820
Can I have seconds, please?

31
00:02:44,600 --> 00:02:46,000
I'm really sorry.

32
00:02:46,000 --> 00:02:49,740
I won't ever neglect my daughter
and go off to pachinko again.

33
00:02:50,180 --> 00:02:52,380
Mariko, let's go out and eat.

34
00:02:52,380 --> 00:02:52,980
Yeah.

35
00:02:54,980 --> 00:02:55,340
Thank you.

36
00:02:56,940 --> 00:02:57,300
Yeah.

37
00:03:05,940 --> 00:03:08,360
Ugh, how totally choberiba.

38
00:03:08,360 --> 00:03:10,600
Naoko, what's wrong?

39
00:03:10,600 --> 00:03:13,500
Reiko-senpai, you have to hear this!

40
00:03:13,500 --> 00:03:16,260
I just wrote someone a parking ticket,

41
00:03:16,260 --> 00:03:19,580
and he tried to pick me up.
And he did it to Senior Komachi, too!

42
00:03:19,580 --> 00:03:23,060
I can't accept flowers like these!

43
00:03:23,060 --> 00:03:27,220
You're the only woman worthy of riding
in the passenger seat of my Porsche.

44
00:03:27,620 --> 00:03:31,580
Roses like these are nothing
but a backdrop next to you.

45
00:03:31,580 --> 00:03:33,120
W-well, do you think so?

46
00:03:33,580 --> 00:03:37,000
How about we go for a drive to Yokohama?

47
00:03:37,540 --> 00:03:40,540
Let's have dinner at a chic
restaurant and watch the sunset.

48
00:03:41,500 --> 00:03:43,340
But I'm still on duty.

49
00:03:44,100 --> 00:03:46,960
A pearl white Porsche, how unusual.

50
00:04:04,300 --> 00:04:05,080
Beep!

51
00:04:06,600 --> 00:04:09,500
If you're that set on getting through,
maybe you've been slipping out early.

52
00:04:10,960 --> 00:04:15,260
I didn't expect a woman who could recognize a pearl-white Porsche,
one of a kind in Japan.

53
00:04:16,000 --> 00:04:16,740
I'm delighted.

54
00:04:16,740 --> 00:04:18,780
Ma'am, ma'am.

55
00:04:18,780 --> 00:04:20,480
You mean "Mademoiselle," right?

56
00:04:20,480 --> 00:04:26,500
Exactly.
You're my ideal Ma'am-ma'am-moiselle.

57
00:04:26,500 --> 00:04:30,580
So this car's passenger seat
was prepared just for you.

58
00:04:31,320 --> 00:04:33,660
Why don't you come for a
drive to Yokohama with me?

59
00:04:34,960 --> 00:04:38,480
Sorry, but I prefer the driver's
seat to the passenger seat.

60
00:04:38,480 --> 00:04:42,360
And you'd do better not to
use words you're not used to.

61
00:04:43,540 --> 00:04:48,860
Right, miss. I forgot to introduce myself.
I'm Reiji Shiratori, the super-rich man.

62
00:04:50,480 --> 00:04:52,040
You want to know what university I went to?

63
00:04:54,740 --> 00:04:56,820
Of course, OK University.

64
00:04:56,820 --> 00:04:58,900
Not that I asked, though.

65
00:04:58,900 --> 00:05:00,100
Let's go.

66
00:05:00,100 --> 00:05:02,680
Pfft.

67
00:05:02,680 --> 00:05:04,420
You want to know where I live?

68
00:05:04,960 --> 00:05:06,500
Of course, Denenchofu.

69
00:05:06,500 --> 00:05:08,360
The lot is 150 tsubo.

70
00:05:08,360 --> 00:05:10,480
What, you're saying it's super amazing?

71
00:05:10,960 --> 00:05:12,300
It's nothing special.

72
00:05:12,300 --> 00:05:15,060
Keep bragging like that forever!

73
00:05:15,220 --> 00:05:15,640
Yeah.

74
00:05:16,060 --> 00:05:18,520
You'd better pay that fine, you octopus!

75
00:05:20,580 --> 00:05:22,900
I won't let an ugly
woman's words reach my ears.

76
00:05:24,840 --> 00:05:27,880
Miss, I have a Porsche, you know.

77
00:05:27,880 --> 00:05:30,400
There's no way you can escape from me.

78
00:05:39,780 --> 00:05:41,580
He's still chasing us.

79
00:05:41,580 --> 00:05:43,840
In a Porsche, he'd catch up in no time.

80
00:05:48,580 --> 00:05:51,020
Don't worry, with that driving,
he won't catch up.

81
00:05:55,020 --> 00:05:57,040
Damn it! Come on, come on, come on!

82
00:05:57,040 --> 00:05:59,740
Can't keep up with my quick gear shifts,
can you?

83
00:05:59,740 --> 00:06:01,020
Come on! Come on! Come on!

84
00:06:04,500 --> 00:06:07,620
I heard there are more and
more women addicted to pachinko.

85
00:06:07,620 --> 00:06:10,320
So there really are mothers like that

86
00:06:11,060 --> 00:06:13,480
It's really a big social problem.

87
00:06:14,920 --> 00:06:16,660
What is it?

88
00:06:17,960 --> 00:06:21,840
Well, I was just surprised to hear the words
"social issues" come out of your mouth, senpai.

89
00:06:21,840 --> 00:06:26,060
Ryotsu, showing an interest in social
issues is a good thing, you know.

90
00:06:27,060 --> 00:06:27,860
I see.

91
00:06:28,380 --> 00:06:32,940
Well, with so many female customers coming in,
we just can't seem to get our cut.

92
00:06:33,600 --> 00:06:35,780
We really need to do something about it.

93
00:06:36,200 --> 00:06:38,020
Bakabon!

94
00:06:38,440 --> 00:06:40,100
You really are something else.

95
00:06:40,100 --> 00:06:40,720
Now.

96
00:06:42,960 --> 00:06:43,820
This sound...

97
00:06:46,100 --> 00:06:47,180
Just as I thought.

98
00:06:47,620 --> 00:06:48,580
Well, this is a problem.

99
00:06:49,200 --> 00:06:51,040
Reiko, what's wrong?

100
00:06:51,040 --> 00:06:53,300
That suave guy driving that Porsche...

101
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:55,140
keeps pestering me and won't leave me alone.

102
00:06:58,000 --> 00:06:59,540
It finally stalled on me!

103
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:02,140
That's enough to make a Porsche cry.

104
00:07:02,140 --> 00:07:03,020
Damn it!

105
00:07:03,020 --> 00:07:04,980
Why did it have to stop?

106
00:07:11,120 --> 00:07:25,760
Aaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaaah!

107
00:07:25,760 --> 00:07:27,620
Glittering diamond-studded Rolux.

108
00:07:28,260 --> 00:07:30,700
Mario Maani jacket and coat.

109
00:07:31,160 --> 00:07:33,100
The tie is Fantix.

110
00:07:33,900 --> 00:07:35,040
Shoes are Herragamo.

111
00:07:36,660 --> 00:07:38,880
All of it, head to toe,
comes to ten million yen.

112
00:07:38,880 --> 00:07:42,560
My name is Reiji Shiratori,
the super-rich man.

113
00:07:44,020 --> 00:07:46,440
Are you some relative of the Super Saiyan?

114
00:07:47,600 --> 00:07:48,940
No!

115
00:07:50,260 --> 00:07:51,680
Just an idiot.

116
00:07:52,280 --> 00:07:53,260
Let's go back, let's go back.

117
00:07:53,260 --> 00:07:53,740
Hey!

118
00:07:56,080 --> 00:07:59,120
You've got some nerve, ignoring me.

119
00:07:59,540 --> 00:08:00,460
I'll give you credit for that.

120
00:08:00,460 --> 00:08:02,060
Barging in uninvited, are you?

121
00:08:02,520 --> 00:08:04,060
I have no use for you.

122
00:08:04,060 --> 00:08:05,220
Step back.

123
00:08:05,220 --> 00:08:07,140
The one I have business with

124
00:08:07,820 --> 00:08:08,220
is you.

125
00:08:08,920 --> 00:08:12,780
You've made Reiji Shiratori fall for you at first sight,
you little devil.

126
00:08:14,200 --> 00:08:15,460
I'm busy today.

127
00:08:15,460 --> 00:08:16,240
See you later.

128
00:08:18,580 --> 00:08:19,580
No, no.

129
00:08:19,580 --> 00:08:21,700
You can't escape from me now.

130
00:08:21,700 --> 00:08:24,920
You're a lucky girl to ride in my Porsche.

131
00:08:26,300 --> 00:08:28,820
Who'd want to ride in a
Porsche that stalls, right?

132
00:08:29,720 --> 00:08:31,920
I came to a full stop at that spot.

133
00:08:31,920 --> 00:08:33,980
It absolutely did not stall.

134
00:08:33,980 --> 00:08:36,880
Alright, don't get so worked up.

135
00:08:37,380 --> 00:08:41,400
Come on, miss,
let's go for a drive in my Porsche.

136
00:08:41,960 --> 00:08:43,500
I'm on duty, so no.

137
00:08:44,200 --> 00:08:46,320
Then how about dinner after your shift?

138
00:08:46,900 --> 00:08:49,060
I have a favorite restaurant in Ginza.

139
00:08:50,200 --> 00:08:51,800
I have plans tonight.

140
00:08:51,800 --> 00:08:53,980
You want to know where my home is?

141
00:08:55,760 --> 00:08:59,000
A thousand yen, 150 grains of Chofu... that's what you said,
right? I just heard it.

142
00:08:59,000 --> 00:09:00,420
Y-yes, that's right.

143
00:09:00,420 --> 00:09:02,180
Your father?

144
00:09:03,400 --> 00:09:04,960
He's started talking to himself.

145
00:09:05,460 --> 00:09:07,100
He's the president of Shiratori Iron Works.

146
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:09,440
Someday,
I'm supposed to become president myself.

147
00:09:09,440 --> 00:09:10,600
Impressive, isn't it?

148
00:09:12,040 --> 00:09:14,240
I told you, you can't escape, young lady.

149
00:09:16,280 --> 00:09:19,400
Shiratori Iron Works is a first-rate company,
you know.

150
00:09:19,800 --> 00:09:22,220
It even runs in TV commercials, doesn't it?

151
00:09:22,220 --> 00:09:25,260
That one where the father
and son talk by the seaside?

152
00:09:25,760 --> 00:09:27,940
You know about it, you poor people?

153
00:09:31,280 --> 00:09:33,580
My father is stubborn and inflexible.

154
00:09:33,580 --> 00:09:37,180
After all, we deal in iron.

155
00:09:37,180 --> 00:09:39,400
You got me there.

156
00:09:45,700 --> 00:09:48,440
Shiratori Iron Works, aiming for tomorrow.

157
00:09:49,020 --> 00:09:51,480
The man in that commercial is my old man.

158
00:09:52,220 --> 00:09:53,200
Yeah, it's amazing, right?

159
00:09:53,760 --> 00:09:56,120
It's memorable, I'll give it that.
It gives you chills.

160
00:09:56,120 --> 00:09:57,140
Shut up!

161
00:09:57,140 --> 00:09:59,080
All you do is complain, complain, complain.

162
00:09:59,540 --> 00:10:02,040
This is why I can't stand super-poor people.

163
00:10:02,040 --> 00:10:03,940
Reiko-san, if you want to get away,

164
00:10:04,280 --> 00:10:06,780
you just need to keep moving to his right,
to his right.

165
00:10:06,780 --> 00:10:07,320
Mm.

166
00:10:08,220 --> 00:10:10,460
You don't even know
the hardships of an heir,

167
00:10:10,840 --> 00:10:12,040
so stop being jealous.

168
00:10:13,400 --> 00:10:15,440
Miss, how many times do I have to say it?

169
00:10:21,360 --> 00:10:24,320
Miss you and me, what, what about

170
00:10:24,320 --> 00:10:28,300
Damn it, don't you dare look down on me!

171
00:10:28,300 --> 00:10:29,940
Argh!

172
00:10:34,300 --> 00:10:36,940
I-I will never give up!

173
00:10:37,840 --> 00:10:40,440
I'll absolutely win your heart.

174
00:10:40,440 --> 00:10:42,400
That guy's still hitting on her.

175
00:10:43,740 --> 00:10:45,880
Miss, please wait for me.

176
00:10:59,980 --> 00:11:02,820
Speaking of which,
I wonder what that Shiratori guy is up to.

177
00:11:03,560 --> 00:11:05,300
Isn't he still in the hospital?

178
00:11:05,700 --> 00:11:09,940
Even though he's just as rich,
he's nothing like Nakagawa or Reiko.

179
00:11:09,940 --> 00:11:11,620
That Shiratori guy...

180
00:11:12,400 --> 00:11:14,940
Could that be because of
your father's influence?

181
00:11:14,940 --> 00:11:16,380
You know about it?

182
00:11:17,060 --> 00:11:20,480
Shiratori Iron Works is a
subcontractor of Daddy's company.

183
00:11:20,480 --> 00:11:22,220
Is that so?

184
00:11:22,600 --> 00:11:26,360
So he came after you without knowing
you're the daughter of the parent company?

185
00:11:26,360 --> 00:11:28,340
What a dimwit.

186
00:11:32,680 --> 00:11:34,320
Speak of the devil.

187
00:11:39,520 --> 00:11:41,700
Still a lousy driver, isn't he.

188
00:11:47,860 --> 00:11:51,520
Aaaah, ugh,
these poor people at the police box...

189
00:11:52,020 --> 00:11:55,880
Hard at work every day You're too far away,
I can't hear you!

190
00:11:56,280 --> 00:11:59,360
Come up to the police box properly! Shut up!

191
00:12:01,680 --> 00:12:07,560
It's not a breakdown, I stopped there on purpose.
Still a creepy way of moving, this guy.

192
00:12:08,680 --> 00:12:15,960
Miss, you'll really come for a drive with me today! I'll get going right away, so no more
"no" from you!

193
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:19,900
You'd better not force yourself
to ride in that Porsche.

194
00:12:19,900 --> 00:12:21,420
H-how rude!

195
00:12:21,740 --> 00:12:22,140
You there!

196
00:12:28,700 --> 00:12:30,900
You're pretty handsome, you know.

197
00:12:30,900 --> 00:12:32,960
Are you perhaps her boyfriend?

198
00:12:34,340 --> 00:12:36,920
Even if you're her boyfriend,
you don't stand a chance.

199
00:12:36,920 --> 00:12:38,580
Because I'm

200
00:12:38,580 --> 00:12:39,740
rich!

201
00:12:40,180 --> 00:12:40,800
handsome!

202
00:12:41,840 --> 00:12:42,640
smart!

203
00:12:43,500 --> 00:12:45,680
Three-for-three, that's me.

204
00:12:46,300 --> 00:12:47,340
And on top of that,

205
00:12:48,580 --> 00:12:51,580
I drive a white reverse Porsche.

206
00:12:51,580 --> 00:12:51,840
Ah

207
00:12:55,140 --> 00:12:56,740
Too much!

208
00:12:56,740 --> 00:13:03,460
Who drew this crappy graffiti with a marker?

209
00:13:03,460 --> 00:13:05,880
This is why I hate coming
to the old downtown.

210
00:13:05,880 --> 00:13:06,640
Yo!

211
00:13:06,640 --> 00:13:07,820
Tattoo Porsche

212
00:13:07,820 --> 00:13:09,680
Shut up, you pauper!

213
00:13:09,680 --> 00:13:10,580
Enough already!

214
00:13:11,400 --> 00:13:12,740
Too close, too close!

215
00:13:12,740 --> 00:13:15,460
Can't you see these wads of cash?

216
00:13:15,460 --> 00:13:16,600
*Pant, pant*

217
00:13:17,920 --> 00:13:21,340
How precious! Seeing money
makes you servile by pure reflex!

218
00:13:22,060 --> 00:13:23,600
Hitting someone with a stack of bills,
no less...

219
00:13:23,600 --> 00:13:27,020
Y-you don't even know the
hardship of inheritance tax!

220
00:13:27,200 --> 00:13:28,680
How much is your salary?

221
00:13:29,680 --> 00:13:31,800
About 220,000 yen...

222
00:13:31,800 --> 00:13:34,520
Then it's the same as one
of these custom-made shoes!

223
00:13:34,960 --> 00:13:38,080
On my salary, I can only buy one shoe?

224
00:13:38,860 --> 00:13:40,800
Somehow, I feel so pitiful...

225
00:13:40,800 --> 00:13:42,080
What's your annual income?

226
00:13:42,560 --> 00:13:43,640
I don't know that!

227
00:13:44,180 --> 00:13:45,560
It's about 7 million yen.

228
00:13:46,560 --> 00:13:49,160
That's the same as this
Rolux Diamond-Kind model!

229
00:13:50,820 --> 00:13:52,360
Whoa, I went and did it again.

230
00:13:52,360 --> 00:13:55,700
Don't underestimate
Super Rich Reiji Shiratori!

231
00:13:56,320 --> 00:13:59,760
Now do you see the difference in level
between you super poor people and me?

232
00:14:03,520 --> 00:14:05,200
Looks like you finally understand.

233
00:14:06,580 --> 00:14:10,480
Come on, hanging around these
paupers will make you turn into one.

234
00:14:11,080 --> 00:14:13,100
Let's go somewhere for a fancy meal,
just you and me.

235
00:14:14,740 --> 00:14:16,940
That's enough out of you!

236
00:14:20,460 --> 00:14:22,580
Uh-oh, Reiko's lost it!

237
00:14:25,120 --> 00:14:26,480
Listening to you go on
and on this whole time -

238
00:14:26,480 --> 00:14:27,640
Stop it, Reiko!

239
00:14:27,640 --> 00:14:29,740
Let go of me, Ryo-chan, let go!

240
00:14:29,740 --> 00:14:30,700
Calm down, Reiko!

241
00:14:31,220 --> 00:14:33,220
Aren't you angry at
being talked to like that?

242
00:14:33,800 --> 00:14:36,600
If it were normal Ryo-chan, you'd have
totally knocked him out by now, wouldn't you?

243
00:14:36,600 --> 00:14:40,600
That's true, but when a guy
like that gets his pride hurt,

244
00:14:40,600 --> 00:14:42,600
there's no telling what he'll do.

245
00:14:43,100 --> 00:14:44,420
Just humor him and have dinner with him.

246
00:14:45,660 --> 00:14:47,520
Of course, not you alone.

247
00:14:47,960 --> 00:14:49,600
Our shift's almost over anyway.

248
00:14:49,600 --> 00:14:52,680
Nakagawa and I will tag
along as your bodyguards.

249
00:14:53,120 --> 00:14:53,480
What?

250
00:14:54,160 --> 00:14:56,740
Are you trying to get
a free meal for yourself?

251
00:14:56,740 --> 00:14:59,980
I'm only coming along as a bodyguard,
you know.

252
00:14:59,980 --> 00:15:01,260
Fine, I get it.

253
00:15:01,960 --> 00:15:03,460
Well, if Ryo-chan's coming along,

254
00:15:03,460 --> 00:15:05,800
all right, it's a deal.

255
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:10,740
Seriously, why do we have to

256
00:15:10,740 --> 00:15:12,400
treat those guys to dinner?

257
00:15:14,020 --> 00:15:14,900
Did you say something?

258
00:15:16,260 --> 00:15:16,652
No, nothing.

259
00:15:16,702 --> 00:15:22,160
I said maybe it'd be nice to let
the poor folks feel rich for once.

260
00:15:23,980 --> 00:15:26,080
My Ferrari could seat four people.

261
00:15:26,080 --> 00:15:29,140
If we tag along in the Ferrari,
his pride will get hurt.

262
00:15:29,140 --> 00:15:31,880
We'll flatter him into paying for the meal.

263
00:15:31,880 --> 00:15:33,740
So to speak, Reiko is the bait.

264
00:15:33,740 --> 00:15:37,040
As expected, super poor people
come up with amazing ideas.

265
00:15:38,160 --> 00:15:40,500
Can't he do something about that driving?

266
00:15:40,620 --> 00:15:42,000
At this rate, we'll be here until dawn.

267
00:15:43,100 --> 00:15:48,140
I know, you see.
Reiko Akimoto, what a lovely name.

268
00:15:48,660 --> 00:15:55,540
So where do you live? Seijō. Isn't that a luxury
residential area second only to Denenchofu?

269
00:15:56,460 --> 00:16:03,000
Do you live with your parents? No,
I live alone. So it's a studio apartment?

270
00:16:03,540 --> 00:16:10,300
Well, it's a 4LDK.
Then the rent must be pretty high, right?

271
00:16:10,780 --> 00:16:13,880
My father bought it for me,
so I don't pay rent.

272
00:16:13,880 --> 00:16:16,775
W-well, you're quite the wealthy one,
aren't you?

273
00:16:16,825 --> 00:16:18,200
Then what about your family home?

274
00:16:18,600 --> 00:16:19,500
It's in Ashiya.

275
00:16:19,500 --> 00:16:21,903
Isn't that Kansai's Denenchofu?

276
00:16:21,953 --> 00:16:25,540
So is the lot about 150 tsubo, like ours?

277
00:16:26,220 --> 00:16:27,740
Maybe a little more.

278
00:16:28,300 --> 00:16:29,100
200 tsubo.

279
00:16:29,100 --> 00:16:30,380
A bit more.

280
00:16:30,380 --> 00:16:32,040
So 300 tsubo?

281
00:16:32,360 --> 00:16:34,060
I'd say around 500 tsubo.

282
00:16:34,060 --> 00:16:35,240
500 tsubo!

283
00:16:39,360 --> 00:16:41,160
Burger's staging it again, the damn fool.

284
00:16:48,300 --> 00:16:49,140
Don't rush it, Reiji.

285
00:16:49,140 --> 00:16:52,360
Even if it's 500 tsubo, it must be deep in
the mountains on the outskirts of Ashiya.

286
00:16:53,380 --> 00:16:55,480
By the way, I'm fine with it.

287
00:16:55,480 --> 00:16:57,100
Which university did you graduate from?

288
00:16:57,420 --> 00:16:58,760
Jouhin University.

289
00:16:58,760 --> 00:16:59,860
I win.

290
00:16:59,860 --> 00:17:03,420
That's a great university full of young ladies,
isn't it?

291
00:17:05,240 --> 00:17:07,080
You get in automatically
through the escalator, right?

292
00:17:07,080 --> 00:17:08,840
I joined at university.

293
00:17:08,840 --> 00:17:12,500
Before that, I was at the Lausanne campus of St.
Coria University.

294
00:17:12,500 --> 00:17:13,860
Never heard of that university.

295
00:17:14,360 --> 00:17:16,780
It was a very strict boarding school.

296
00:17:16,780 --> 00:17:17,840
You've never heard of it?

297
00:17:18,740 --> 00:17:20,020
Of course I know.

298
00:17:20,020 --> 00:17:22,060
Wasn't it Chiba, I think?

299
00:17:22,180 --> 00:17:23,300
It's Switzerland, actually.

300
00:17:23,300 --> 00:17:24,140
Switzerland!

301
00:17:28,580 --> 00:17:31,040
Shiratori, should I take over driving?

302
00:17:31,920 --> 00:17:32,680
I'm fine.

303
00:17:33,140 --> 00:17:36,060
But there's a huge traffic
jam building up behind us.

304
00:17:36,540 --> 00:17:39,260
Move it, you idiot!
Get going, you damn dumbass!

305
00:17:39,260 --> 00:17:41,080
Idiot!

306
00:17:41,180 --> 00:17:41,760
Hurry!

307
00:17:49,940 --> 00:17:51,500
Looks like Reiko took over the wheel.

308
00:17:51,500 --> 00:17:53,940
Reiko has an A-class license, after all.

309
00:17:54,400 --> 00:17:57,260
Driver,
please keep up so we don't lose them.

310
00:17:57,260 --> 00:17:57,860
Yes.

311
00:18:13,340 --> 00:18:14,660
This is too good.

312
00:18:23,400 --> 00:18:26,940
I come here often,
but it's hard to get a table.

313
00:18:26,940 --> 00:18:29,060
Ms. Akimoto.

314
00:18:30,060 --> 00:18:32,500
And Mr. Nakagawa is with you as well.

315
00:18:33,000 --> 00:18:33,940
Welcome.

316
00:18:33,940 --> 00:18:34,800
Thanks.

317
00:18:35,260 --> 00:18:36,540
This way, please.

318
00:18:36,940 --> 00:18:39,680
Hey, why aren't you greeting me?

319
00:18:39,680 --> 00:18:42,740
Excuse me, but who are you?

320
00:18:43,060 --> 00:18:46,260
How rude! I'm Reiji Shiratori,
the one who made the reservation!

321
00:18:46,620 --> 00:18:48,360
And I'm the one paying, you know!

322
00:18:53,320 --> 00:18:54,540
I'm terribly sorry about that.

323
00:18:54,540 --> 00:18:56,820
Since the reservation was for two,

324
00:18:56,820 --> 00:18:59,620
we'll be seating you at a table for four.

325
00:19:00,240 --> 00:19:01,580
Right this way, please.

326
00:19:02,680 --> 00:19:05,400
But apart from Reiko,

327
00:19:06,400 --> 00:19:11,040
I'm surprised you've been to a five-star luxury restaurant like this,
Ryo-chan.

328
00:19:11,040 --> 00:19:13,300
Just once or twice.

329
00:19:13,820 --> 00:19:16,460
What, you've only been here that few times?

330
00:19:16,940 --> 00:19:18,200
Don't scare me like that.

331
00:19:18,800 --> 00:19:19,980
Once a week, actually.

332
00:19:20,880 --> 00:19:23,100
Hey, super rich man, you're unbeatable!

333
00:19:28,560 --> 00:19:29,800
It's not about the number of times.

334
00:19:29,800 --> 00:19:34,020
What matters is how much
money you spend at once.

335
00:19:35,620 --> 00:19:38,080
Order whatever you like, my friend.

336
00:19:38,080 --> 00:19:41,280
Super rich people really
do have different tickets

337
00:19:41,280 --> 00:19:42,400
Is that so?

338
00:19:44,180 --> 00:19:50,440
We researched this place on the Tokyo Date Map,
and you turn out to be a regular.

339
00:19:51,160 --> 00:19:53,860
Have you decided on your order, sir?

340
00:19:55,700 --> 00:19:56,600
Order

341
00:20:01,300 --> 00:20:03,900
I can't read it, so I'll just
have everything written in French.

342
00:20:04,700 --> 00:20:05,740
What are you doing?

343
00:20:06,400 --> 00:20:09,580
Everything here is delicious, you know.

344
00:20:10,100 --> 00:20:11,180
I'm just torn between them.

345
00:20:11,180 --> 00:20:12,300
What should I do?

346
00:20:12,720 --> 00:20:14,140
At this point,
everything from the top of the menu!

347
00:20:14,880 --> 00:20:18,220
Wouldn't the chef's omakase course,
number 20, be good?

348
00:20:18,920 --> 00:20:20,660
We're in trouble now.

349
00:20:21,120 --> 00:20:23,820
I was just about to choose that one too.

350
00:20:23,820 --> 00:20:26,860
Super rich people really do see eye to eye,
don't they.

351
00:20:29,860 --> 00:20:31,200
I'll go with that too.

352
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:32,380
I'll have the same.

353
00:20:32,380 --> 00:20:33,320
Very good, sir.

354
00:20:36,200 --> 00:20:38,240
Ms. Akimoto and Mr. Nakagawa.

355
00:20:39,560 --> 00:20:42,000
Well, welcome, all of you.

356
00:20:42,560 --> 00:20:45,500
If you'd like, we have a VIP room available.

357
00:20:45,500 --> 00:20:49,800
Whoops, I guess they've figured out I'm
the vice president of Shiratori Iron Works.

358
00:20:50,260 --> 00:20:51,540
Let's get right to it, then.

359
00:20:53,340 --> 00:20:54,680
This is fine here.

360
00:20:55,260 --> 00:20:56,580
I see, madam.

361
00:20:58,320 --> 00:20:59,980
Wh-hey, w-wait!

362
00:20:59,980 --> 00:21:01,900
I already told you we're going, damn it!

363
00:21:03,320 --> 00:21:06,980
Come on, he's a super-rich guy.
Don't worry about it, don't worry about it.

364
00:21:11,180 --> 00:21:14,080
I wanted to try eating in the
commoners' seats for a change.

365
00:21:14,520 --> 00:21:16,280
Is it all right if I order a steak too?

366
00:21:16,720 --> 00:21:17,820
Please, please.

367
00:21:18,240 --> 00:21:20,240
Waiter, one more steak.

368
00:21:20,240 --> 00:21:21,920
Ryo-chan, you really are something.

369
00:21:21,920 --> 00:21:27,460
For the chef's course,
I'd recommend a Bordeaux from 1982.

370
00:21:27,980 --> 00:21:31,020
Wouldn't the 1983 be better than the 1982?

371
00:21:31,020 --> 00:21:34,360
Mr. Nakagawa, you certainly know your wines.

372
00:21:34,360 --> 00:21:38,220
See?! I'm the super-rich
one who's paying here!

373
00:21:38,500 --> 00:21:40,100
Why aren't you asking me?!

374
00:21:41,100 --> 00:21:44,040
You don't have to ask him instead of me!

375
00:21:44,400 --> 00:21:48,000
Why, why does everyone keep ignoring me?

376
00:21:48,540 --> 00:21:49,420
Hey, Reiji.

377
00:21:49,420 --> 00:21:51,620
Dad.

378
00:21:51,620 --> 00:21:53,880
The company president's son?

379
00:21:54,180 --> 00:21:56,300
Yeah, just wait a moment.

380
00:21:57,060 --> 00:21:58,720
I didn't expect to see you here too.

381
00:21:58,720 --> 00:22:01,200
You're as lively as ever too, Dad.

382
00:22:01,200 --> 00:22:03,100
Don't tell your mom, though.

383
00:22:06,500 --> 00:22:08,160
She's a nice one, isn't she?

384
00:22:08,160 --> 00:22:09,840
Which club is she from?

385
00:22:09,840 --> 00:22:10,940
Ugh, come on.

386
00:22:10,940 --> 00:22:12,880
Unlike you, Dad,

387
00:22:12,880 --> 00:22:15,100
I don't hit on the hostesses at Domia.

388
00:22:15,660 --> 00:22:18,460
But I can have her fall for me in no time,
you know.

389
00:22:20,240 --> 00:22:21,300
Let me introduce you.

390
00:22:21,300 --> 00:22:21,740
This is...

391
00:22:24,040 --> 00:22:25,980
Good evening, Uncle.

392
00:22:28,100 --> 00:22:29,460
You know him?

393
00:22:30,240 --> 00:22:31,200
Y-you!

394
00:22:32,500 --> 00:22:35,660
This lady is the daughter of Akimoto Kōeki,
you idiot!

395
00:22:35,780 --> 00:22:37,400
You and I are as different
as the moon and a turtle!

396
00:22:38,100 --> 00:22:38,604
Miss,

397
00:22:38,654 --> 00:22:42,120
I'm terribly sorry for my
good-for-nothing son's rudeness!

398
00:22:42,860 --> 00:22:45,560
O-oh, sir, there's no need to go that far...

399
00:22:46,080 --> 00:22:47,500
Not at all.

400
00:22:47,500 --> 00:22:50,880
Our company exists only thanks to Akimoto Kōeki,
after all.

401
00:22:51,880 --> 00:22:55,760
Dad, miss, even if Shiratori didn't know, isn't that a bit much?
Please, let's...

402
00:22:56,500 --> 00:22:57,860
I don't mind at all.

403
00:22:58,240 --> 00:23:00,500
Even a supercar owner pales in comparison.

404
00:23:02,640 --> 00:23:05,380
I wonder how Shiratori's doing,
we haven't seen him since.

405
00:23:05,380 --> 00:23:07,440
We really did him wrong.

406
00:23:07,960 --> 00:23:09,645
It's not your fault,

407
00:23:09,695 --> 00:23:12,220
since he's the one who came up to us.

408
00:23:12,640 --> 00:23:13,000
But...

409
00:23:13,800 --> 00:23:14,980
Hey, gentlemen.

410
00:23:14,980 --> 00:23:16,220
You're...

411
00:23:17,240 --> 00:23:18,600
S-Shiratori-san!

412
00:23:18,600 --> 00:23:20,680
What happened to you, dressed like that?

413
00:23:22,460 --> 00:23:27,260
After that, Dad was so moved that he gave me everything,
and I became a super-duper pauper.

414
00:23:27,260 --> 00:23:28,580
I'm really sorry.

415
00:23:30,080 --> 00:23:31,500
No need to worry.

416
00:23:31,500 --> 00:23:36,140
I'll climb back up soon and become a super-duper rich man again,
you'll see.

417
00:23:36,640 --> 00:23:37,940
Until then, farewell!

418
00:23:41,700 --> 00:23:42,740
He's a good guy, this one.

419
00:23:42,740 --> 00:23:46,520
Hurry up and become a super-duper rich man again,
and treat us to a meal!

420
00:23:48,900 --> 00:23:50,720
Yo, super-duper rich man!

421
00:24:03,980 --> 00:24:06,340
Why am I digging a tunnel, you ask?

422
00:24:07,620 --> 00:24:10,100
It's a prison break,
like in the movies, a prison break!

423
00:24:10,100 --> 00:24:14,460
The Chief locked me in a cage,
so I'm digging my way out, that's the plan!

424
00:24:14,820 --> 00:24:16,260
Just you wait, Chief.

425
00:24:16,520 --> 00:24:18,320
I'm coming for my revenge now.

426
00:24:18,320 --> 00:24:20,840
Next time: Ryo-san's Great Escape.

427
00:24:20,840 --> 00:24:21,880
See you then.

428
00:24:29,100 --> 00:24:32,700
Even if you stop the clock,

429
00:24:34,480 --> 00:24:37,760
time keeps moving on.

430
00:24:39,500 --> 00:24:42,720
Don't keep that sour face,

431
00:24:44,260 --> 00:24:48,000
let's laugh it off and keep living.

432
00:24:50,280 --> 00:24:57,920
Even if today is rainy,

433
00:24:59,480 --> 00:25:03,460
tomorrow will be sunny.

434
00:25:03,460 --> 00:25:08,620
Bye-bye, let's wave goodbye.

435
00:25:08,620 --> 00:25:13,860
Unpleasant things, sayonara!

436
00:25:13,860 --> 00:25:21,500
Oh yeah, let's try living the way we like.

437
00:25:21,500 --> 00:25:23,940
Good things will come.

438
00:25:24,480 --> 00:25:30,240
Outside the door, the sun is calling to us.

439
00:25:38,620 --> 00:25:41,780
Thanks for watching.

